(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Ice Yield Surface (p-q space): Current vs. Smooth Candidates", "Title"],

Cell["\<\
Compares two yield surfaces for fractured/crushed ice in (p, q) \
stress-invariant space:
1. Current: min of the elliptic cap and the Drucker-Prager line \
(Q_From_Yield_Surcace in kernels.cu).
2. Ellipse and DP line blended via a smooth-min with a tunable exponent \
(\"flipped exponent\", a reciprocal power mean), which coincides with the \
current DP line near the threshold and saturates toward the ellipse for \
larger p, converging to the exact current curve as the exponent grows.

The flipped-exponent candidate is plotted with its full formula written \
directly in the Plot call. Everything below is static plots -- edit the \
numbers in the Input cells directly and re-evaluate to try different \
values.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Parameters (from _input_data/nares_7k/simulation.json)", "Section"],

Cell["\<\
All nares_*k configs currently share these values. UseLiveIceStrength is \
true at runtime, so the real per-point fractured-shear-strength ceiling \
is the dynamic idx_xi * IceShearStrengthFracturedRatio, not a fixed \
constant -- IceShearStrengthFractured (the flat fallback constant) is \
used below purely as a representative qmax for visualizing the SHAPE of \
the surface.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell["\<\
pminVal = -3.5*10^5;          (* -IceTensileStrength *)
pmaxVal = 100*10^6;           (* IceCompressiveStrength *)
dpThresholdVal = -1.0*10^3;   (* DP_threshold_p *)
dpPhiVal = 55;                (* DP_phi, degrees *)
qmaxFracturedVal = 4.5*10^5;  (* IceShearStrengthFractured, flat stand-in *)\
\>", "Input"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Yield-Surface Definitions", "Section"],

Cell["\<\
qEllipse[p_, pmin_, pmax_, qmax_] := 2 Sqrt[Max[0, (pmax - p) (p - pmin)]] qmax/(pmax - pmin)

qDP[p_, threshold_, phiDeg_] := Max[0, (p - threshold) Tan[phiDeg Degree]]

(* Candidate 1: what we currently run -- exact port of Q_From_Yield_Surcace in kernels.cu *)
qCurrent[p_, pmin_, pmax_, qmax_, threshold_, phiDeg_] := If[p > pmax || p < threshold, 0, Min[qEllipse[p, pmin, pmax, qmax], qDP[p, threshold, phiDeg]]]\
\>", "Input"],

Cell["\<\
Alternative -- smooth-min via \"flipped exponent\" (reciprocal power \
mean): SoftMin[a, b; n] = (a^-n + b^-n)^(-1/n) = a b/(a^n + b^n)^(1/n). \
As n -> Infinity this reduces exactly to Min[a, b], today's hard corner. \
Near p = threshold, qDP -> 0 while qEllipse stays finite, so the \
softmin automatically tracks qDP -- same value and slope as the \
current DP line, with no forcing needed. Past the crossover point qDP \
exceeds qEllipse and the softmin saturates toward qEllipse instead of \
growing without bound.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell["\<\
qFlippedExponent[p_, pmin_, pmax_, qmax_, threshold_, phiDeg_, nExp_] := Module[{a, b}, a = qEllipse[p, pmin, pmax, qmax]; b = qDP[p, threshold, phiDeg]; If[p > pmax || p < threshold, 0, If[a == 0 && b == 0, 0, a b/(a^nExp + b^nExp)^(1/nExp)]]]\
\>", "Input"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Flipped-Exponent Candidate", "Section"],

Cell["\<\
Own plot, current surface shown for reference. The full soft-min \
expression a b/(a^n + b^n)^(1/n) is written out directly in the Plot \
call below (a = qEllipse[p, ...], b = qDP[p, ...]) rather than going \
through the qFlippedExponent[...] helper -- edit the n -> 5 below \
directly to try other steepness values.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell["\<\
Plot[
  {qCurrent[p, pminVal, pmaxVal, qmaxFracturedVal, dpThresholdVal, dpPhiVal],
   With[{a = qEllipse[p, pminVal, pmaxVal, qmaxFracturedVal],
         b = qDP[p, dpThresholdVal, dpPhiVal], n = 5},
     a b/(a^n + b^n)^(1/n)]},
  {p, -100000, 400000},
  PlotRange -> {{-100000, 400000}, {0, 70000}},
  PlotLegends -> {\"Current (hard min)\", \"Flipped-exponent soft-min, n = 5\"},
  PlotStyle -> {Directive[Black, Thick], Directive[RGBColor[0.85, 0.2, 0.2], Thick]},
  Frame -> True, FrameLabel -> {\"p  (Pa)\", \"q  (Pa)\"},
  ImageSize -> 650, PlotPoints -> 200]\
\>", "Input"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Flipped-Exponent Multiplier Alone (Without the Ellipse)", "Section"],

Cell["\<\
a b/(a^n + b^n)^(1/n) factors as qEllipse(p) * M(p), where M(p) = \
b/(a^n + b^n)^(1/n) is the multiplier actually applied to the ellipse. \
Plotted alone below (NOT multiplied by the ellipse), so its bare shape \
is visible on its own axis (0 to ~1, dimensionless) rather than in \
stress units. Note M(p) depends on the actual shapes of qEllipse(p) \
and qDP(p) both (not just a fixed function of p alone), so it is not a \
plain, universal S-curve.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell["\<\
Plot[
  With[{a = qEllipse[p, pminVal, pmaxVal, qmaxFracturedVal],
        b = qDP[p, dpThresholdVal, dpPhiVal], n = 5},
    b/(a^n + b^n)^(1/n)],
  {p, -100000, 400000},
  PlotRange -> {{-100000, 400000}, {0, 1.1}},
  PlotStyle -> Directive[RGBColor[0.85, 0.2, 0.2], Thick],
  Frame -> True, FrameLabel -> {\"p  (Pa)\", \"multiplier M(p)\"},
  PlotLabel -> \"Flipped-exponent multiplier alone, n = 5\",
  ImageSize -> 650, PlotPoints -> 200]\
\>", "Input"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Full-Domain Context", "Section"],

Cell["\<\
The interesting transition region above is a tiny sliver of the full \
domain -- IceCompressiveStrength (100 MPa) is far larger than any \
pressure the yield surface actually needs to resolve interestingly, so \
the ellipse's true peak sits far off to the right.

No qCurrent/qEllipse/qDP calls below -- the whole expression is spelled \
out directly: the elliptic-cap term (2*Sqrt[(pmax-p)(p-pmin)]*qmax/ \
(pmax-pmin) -- what gets multiplied by qmax) and the DP-line term \
(Max[0, (p-threshold)*Tan[phi]]), combined with Min[...] and clamped to \
0 outside [DP_threshold_p, pmax] -- an exact, self-contained port of \
Q_From_Yield_Surcace in kernels.cu.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell["\<\
Plot[
  If[p > pmaxVal || p < dpThresholdVal, 0,
    Min[
      2 Sqrt[Max[0, (pmaxVal - p) (p - pminVal)]] qmaxFracturedVal/(pmaxVal - pminVal),
      Max[0, (p - dpThresholdVal) Tan[dpPhiVal Degree]]
    ]
  ],
  {p, pminVal, pmaxVal},
  Frame -> True, FrameLabel -> {\"p  (Pa)\", \"q  (Pa)\"},
  PlotLabel -> \"Current yield surface over its full domain (context)\",
  ImageSize -> 650]\
\>", "Input"]
}, Open  ]]

}, Open  ]]
},
WindowSize->{1385.25, 759},
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb"
]
(* End of Notebook Content *)
